---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { site, disclosure } from '../site.config';
import { feedReviewedDate } from '../lib/feed';
---
<Article
  title="How we rank"
  description="How Bolivia Unpacked orders its operator rankings: only by the Tourground directory rank, never by payment, verified companies only."
  path="/how-we-rank/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'How we rank', path: '/how-we-rank/' }]}
  published={site.launchDate}
  reviewed={feedReviewedDate()}
  sources={[{ url: 'https://tourground.com', label: 'Tourground directory export (company data feed)' }]}
  rail={false}
  kicker="Method"
  lede={disclosure.rankingStatement}
>
  <h2>The rules</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>One source.</strong> Company facts and ranks come only from the Tourground directory export. This site never edits them by hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Verified only.</strong> {disclosure.verifiedOnlyStatement}</li>
    <li><strong>Order comes from the rank field.</strong> Each company has a rank for Bolivia in the directory. Every list on this site shows companies in that order. We do not reorder, boost or demote anyone.</li>
    <li><strong>Lists are filters, not new rankings.</strong> A list such as "Amazon" shows only the verified companies whose directory entry includes that type of trip, still in directory rank order. A position number on a list is the company's place within that list.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment never counts.</strong> No company can pay for a better rank or a place on a list.</li>
    <li><strong>Founder-owned brands follow the same rules.</strong> They are labelled "{disclosure.founderOwnedLabel}" wherever they appear.</li>
    <li><strong>Thin is fine.</strong> If few companies are verified, lists stay short. We never pad them.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Paid placements</h2>
  <p>{disclosure.paidExplainer} They carry the label "{disclosure.paidLabel}". There are no paid placements on the site at present.</p>
  <h2>Links</h2>
  <p>Companies on the Platinum tier may link to their own website. Those links are paid and marked <code>rel="{disclosure.paidLinkRel}"</code>. All other companies link only to their Tourground profile page.</p>
  <h2>Tiers</h2>
  <p>{disclosure.tierExplainer}</p>
  <h2>Updates and removals</h2>
  <p>The site is rebuilt from the latest directory export. A company removed from the directory, or no longer verified, disappears from every page in the next build.</p>
</Article>
